# LABS 1–2: Run npm install, then npm run dev in the repository root.
# With VS Code's REST Client extension, click Send Request above one request.
# In a browser, append each GET path to your running server's URL.
# For a client outside Codespaces, replace baseUrl with your forwarded port URL.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Lab 1: Home route — expected JSON: {"message":"Hello World!"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Lab 2: Route parameter — expected text: Hi, Adzan
GET {{baseUrl}}/hello/Adzan

### Lab 2: Query strings — expected firstName John and lastName Wick
GET {{baseUrl}}/echo?firstName=John&lastName=Wick

### HANDS ON 1: Difference is n1 - n2 — expected text: 11
GET {{baseUrl}}/difference/15/4

### Difference with a negative value — expected text: -8
GET {{baseUrl}}/difference/-5/3

### Difference with a decimal value — expected text: 2.5
GET {{baseUrl}}/difference/7.5/5

### Invalid numeric input — expected 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/difference/hello/5

### HANDS ON 2: Scream — expected text: HELLO ADZAN
GET {{baseUrl}}/scream?message=hello&recipient=Adzan

### A space in the message is encoded as %20 — expected: HELLO THERE ADZAN
GET {{baseUrl}}/scream?message=hello%20there&recipient=Adzan

### Missing recipient — expected 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/scream?message=hello

### Missing echo query key — expected 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/echo?firstName=John

### An unknown route — expected 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/not-a-route
